cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data, please cite them as below, together with the article and the benchmark of D'Ambrosio et al. (2023)."
title: "Data for “Exact swap evaluation for convex set-count penalties: a GPU tabu search for the knapsack problem with forfeit sets”"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "García"
    given-names: "José"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3126-8352"
    affiliation: "Pontificia Universidad Católica de Valparaíso"
  - family-names: "Rojas-Valdivia"
    given-names: "Luis"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-8935-7595"
    affiliation: "Pontificia Universidad Católica de Valparaíso"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/rubincus/kpfs-copts-gpu-results"
abstract: >-
  Data of the article "Exact swap evaluation for convex set-count penalties: a GPU tabu search for the knapsack
  problem with forfeit sets": the new instances (KPFS-L with n = 2000, bridge rehabilitation programs built from the
  2025 National Bridge Inventory and maintenance windows of a computing cluster built from the Alibaba cluster trace
  v2018, with and without split applications), the best solution found for each of the 600 benchmark instances and
  the 60 KPFS-L instances, the records of every run of the computational study, the reports of the analyses and a
  solution verifier.
keywords:
  - knapsack problem with forfeit sets
  - tabu search
  - GPU computing
  - benchmark instances
  - combinatorial optimization
